[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 703,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 466,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107383,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 466,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Ossifying renal tumour of infancy (ORTI) is an intracalyceal neoplasm composed of a combination of osteoid, osteoblastic cells, and spindle cells.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:04:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 704,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 467,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107384,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 467,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8967/0 Ossifying renal tumour of infancy</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:04:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 705,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 468,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107385,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 468,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F35 &amp; XH3SR2 Benign neoplasm of urinary organs &amp; Ossifying renal tumour</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:04:17"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 706,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 469,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107386,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 469,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:04:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 707,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 470,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107387,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 470,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:04:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 708,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 471,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107388,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 471,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Renal pelvis</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:04:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 709,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 472,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107389,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 472,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>ORTI has no specific clinical presentation, but most patients present with gross haematuria and a calcified mass protruding into the renal pelvis on imaging. No association with any other renal tumour type or syndrome has been published.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:04:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 710,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 473,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107390,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 473,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours are extremely rare, with only about 25&nbsp;cases published in the literature. There is a clear male predominance (M:F&nbsp;ratio: 7:1), and patients are between 6&nbsp;days and 2.5&nbsp;years old {27633911; 30425880}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:04:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 711,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 474,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107391,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 474,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:04:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 712,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 475,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107392,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 475,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:04:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 719,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 482,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107393,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 482,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours are well circumscribed and measure 10&ndash;60&nbsp;mm in diameter. Almost all tumours show signs of calcification on imaging studies and this is also reflected in the gross appearance.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:04:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 713,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 476,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107394,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 476,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>ORTIs are composed of two types of cells: osteoblast-like cells that are located between and around areas of osteoid, and a spindle cell (blastema-like) component found mostly at the periphery of the tumour. Both osteoblast-like cells and spindle cells are bland, without features of malignancy. The osteoblast-like cells are almost always immunopositive for EMA and vimentin.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:04:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 714,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 477,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107395,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 477,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:04:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 715,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 478,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107396,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 478,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Two different papers have now described 5&nbsp;cases of ORTI with clonal trisomy&nbsp;4, so this seems to be a relevant and recurrent molecular abnormality {22976287; 27633911}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:04:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 718,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 481,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107397,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 481,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> the typical histological combination of osteoid, osteoblastic cells, and spindle cells is required to make the diagnosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:04:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 716,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 479,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107398,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 479,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>All tumours are limited to the kidney and are regarded as benign lesions. No particular staging protocol applies.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:04:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 717,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 480,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107399,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 259,
        "headingId": 480,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This is a benign tumour for which conservative surgical management is sufficient. Outcome has been uniformly favourable.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:04:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]